An oil delivery assembly for a planetary gear unit comprises:

- a planetary gear mechanism having a cylindrical member that rotates with a carrier supporting planetary gears, the cylindrical member being provided with a lubricant inlet;
- a ring-shaped member in sliding contact with the cylindrical member and having a lubricant supply channel connected to the lubricant inlet;
- two sealing rings mounted on either the cylindrical member or the ring-shaped member on axially opposite sides of the lubricant inlet;
- bypass channels that route lubricant around the respective sealing rings; and
- two pressure-reducing mechanisms, each of which restricts lubricant flow between the cylindrical and ring-shaped members, the mechanisms being positioned either between the lubricant inlet and the respective sealing rings or outward of those sealing rings.
